# Contract: `Failure` (`lib/core/network/failure.dart`)

The typed failure every repository's `Either<Failure, T>` resolves to on the `Left` side
(RNF09, FR-004). Domain-layer code only — no Flutter import.

```dart
sealed class Failure extends Equatable {
  const Failure({required this.message, required this.requestId});
  final String message;
  final String requestId;
  bool get retryable;
  String get code;
  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [code, message, requestId];
}

class AuthExpiredFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => false; String get code => 'AUTH_EXPIRED'; }
class AuthInvalidFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => false; String get code => 'AUTH_INVALID'; }
class NetworkTimeoutFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => true;  String get code => 'NETWORK_TIMEOUT'; }
class NetworkOfflineFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => true;  String get code => 'NETWORK_OFFLINE'; }
class ValidationFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => false; String get code => 'VALIDATION_ERROR'; }
class PiiCheckFailedFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => true;  String get code => 'PII_CHECK_FAILED'; }
class EmbeddingFailedFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => true;  String get code => 'EMBEDDING_FAILED'; }
class AiGenerationTimeoutFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => true;  String get code => 'AI_GENERATION_TIMEOUT'; }
class NotFoundFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => false; String get code => 'NOT_FOUND'; }
class RateLimitedFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => true;  String get code => 'RATE_LIMITED'; }
class ExportEmptyPeriodFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => false; String get code => 'EXPORT_EMPTY_PERIOD'; }
class PayloadTooLargeFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => false; String get code => 'PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE'; }
class OcrNoTextFailure extends Failure { bool get retryable => false; String get code => 'OCR_NO_TEXT'; }
```

`ErrorMapper.fromResponse(Map<String, dynamic> body)` performs the exhaustive `code` → subtype
switch; an unrecognized `code` is a contract violation (the taxonomy is closed per
error-taxonomy.md) and is treated as a defensive `ValidationFailure` rather than thrown, keeping
FR-003's "never an unhandled crash" guarantee even against a future backend regression.

## Who depends on this

Every repository in every feature, present and future. UI code branches on `failure.retryable` to
choose a retry affordance vs. a terminal error message (FR-004, FR-015), and on `runtimeType` (or a
`when`/`switch` pattern) to choose the exact message shown — F000's own screens only branch on
`AuthExpiredFailure`, `AuthInvalidFailure`, `NetworkTimeoutFailure`, `NetworkOfflineFailure`,
`ValidationFailure`, `RateLimitedFailure`; the other seven are reachable only from endpoints later
units add.

# Contract: `SessionRepository` (`lib/features/session/domain/repositories/session_repository.dart`)

Domain-layer interface owning the session lifecycle: launch-time check, silent refresh, and
reading/clearing the stored session. `SessionBloc` depends on this and on nothing in
`session/data/` or `auth/data/` directly (RNF06).

```dart
abstract class SessionRepository {
  Future<Either<Failure, Session>> checkSession();     // GET auth-session, using the stored accessToken
  Future<Either<Failure, Session>> refresh();           // POST auth-refresh, using the stored refreshToken
  Future<void> persist(Session session);                 // write-through to SecureTokenStorage
  Future<void> clear();                                   // logout / failed-refresh cleanup
  Future<bool> hasStoredSession();                        // true iff a refreshToken is present on device
}
```

- **`checkSession`** → FR-009's first step. `Left(AuthExpiredFailure)` is the expected, non-error
  trigger for the caller (`CheckSessionUseCase`) to then call `refresh()` — not itself a terminal
  failure shown to the user.
- **`refresh`** → FR-009's renewal step, also reused for the silent-refresh-before-overlay path of
  FR-013 (User Story 5) and for any later unit's authenticated call that comes back
  `AUTH_EXPIRED`. On `Right`, calls `persist()` internally before returning.
- **`persist`/`clear`** → thin wrappers over `SecureTokenStorage`; exposed on the repository (not
  the data source) so the domain layer's use cases never import `storage/` directly.
- **`hasStoredSession`** → lets `CheckSessionUseCase` skip the network call entirely when there is
  nothing to check (Edge Cases / User Story 3 scenario 2: no stored session → straight to login,
  no call made).

## `CheckSessionUseCase` (orchestration, domain layer)

```dart
Future<SessionStatus> call() async {
  if (!await repo.hasStoredSession()) return SessionStatus.unauthenticated;
  final checked = await repo.checkSession();
  return checked.match(
    (failure) => failure is AuthExpiredFailure
        ? _tryRefresh()
        : SessionStatus.networkError(failure),      // R7 — splash retry affordance, not a route change
    (session) => SessionStatus.authenticated(session),
  );
}

Future<SessionStatus> _tryRefresh() async {
  final refreshed = await repo.refresh();
  return refreshed.match(
    (failure) async { await repo.clear(); return SessionStatus.unauthenticated; },
    (session) => SessionStatus.authenticated(session),
  );
}
```

This single use case is what `SplashPage`/`SessionBloc` calls — it is the only place FR-009's
"renew first, then route" rule is implemented, so later units never re-derive it.

## Who depends on this

`SessionBloc` (splash routing, FR-010; expired-session overlay trigger, FR-013/FR-014). Every later
unit that makes an authenticated call and receives `AuthExpiredFailure` calls `SessionRepository
.refresh()` the same way, through this interface — never by re-implementing the refresh call.

